1
00:00:18,367 --> 00:00:23,305
So now, may I call on for our next item,
Ms. Florence Dela Cruz?

2
00:00:23,305 --> 00:00:24,439
For this item,

3
00:00:24,439 --> 00:00:28,811
Florence will be cooking you a private dinner
in a set-up by the beach.

4
00:00:28,811 --> 00:00:31,546
So, Ms. Florence...

5
00:00:33,415 --> 00:00:35,333
Let's get this bidding started.

6
00:00:35,334 --> 00:00:38,294
Private dinner cooked by Ms. Florence.

7
00:00:38,294 --> 00:00:41,206
Anyone?

8
00:00:41,206 --> 00:00:43,307
One million pesos.

9
00:00:44,710 --> 00:00:47,813
And if you're thinking to outbid me,

10
00:00:47,813 --> 00:00:50,148
don't try anymore.

11
00:00:50,148 --> 00:00:53,085
Because I won't waste this chance

12
00:00:53,085 --> 00:00:56,020
to be with an important person to me.

13
00:00:56,755 --> 00:01:00,792
I won't waste the chance
to be with you again, Florence.

14
00:01:06,498 --> 00:01:07,954
Florence!

15
00:01:08,967 --> 00:01:10,602
And what went into your mind earlier?

16
00:01:10,602 --> 00:01:12,383
Why did you make a bid?

17
00:01:12,383 --> 00:01:15,641
Didn't you even think how Antonia would feel?

18
00:01:15,641 --> 00:01:17,976
Antonia and I are over.

19
00:01:17,976 --> 00:01:22,281
So you called it quits again,
and now, you're going after me?

20
00:01:22,281 --> 00:01:25,684
What?
You'll use me again to make her jealous?

21
00:01:25,684 --> 00:01:26,985
Is that it?

22
00:01:26,985 --> 00:01:29,721
Nero, I don't want anymore.

23
00:01:29,721 --> 00:01:32,858
I don't want to expect. I don't want to hope.

24
00:01:32,858 --> 00:01:36,928
So please, don't play with my heart.

25
00:01:39,765 --> 00:01:43,502
It's you who said that Florence is our cook,

26
00:01:43,502 --> 00:01:46,705
and it's not good to see
that both Ferells are fighting because of her.

27
00:01:46,705 --> 00:01:49,274
Sit together and talk.

28
00:01:49,274 --> 00:01:51,910
Man-to-man, from one Ferell to another.

29
00:01:51,910 --> 00:01:54,446
I don't care what others would say.

30
00:01:54,446 --> 00:01:57,282
My God, dude, you're both Ferells.

31
00:01:57,282 --> 00:01:59,584
Have you forgotten what Grandfather said?

32
00:01:59,584 --> 00:02:04,589
That if we, Ferells, have a problem,
we fix it, together.

33
00:02:04,589 --> 00:02:07,426
That's right. Just fix that problem.

34
00:02:07,426 --> 00:02:09,995
The last thing we want
is us tearing each other apart

35
00:02:09,995 --> 00:02:12,363
because of Florence.

36
00:02:16,001 --> 00:02:19,671
Florence? What happened?

37
00:02:19,671 --> 00:02:21,606
Is there a problem?

38
00:02:27,879 --> 00:02:29,314
<i>Florence is here.</i>

39
00:02:29,314 --> 00:02:31,817
<i>The kid will spend the night here.</i>

40
00:02:31,817 --> 00:02:33,852
<i>But don't worry, she's safe here,</i>

41
00:02:33,852 --> 00:02:38,756
away from your grandsons whose relationship
is a bit complicated with her.

42
00:03:43,770 --> 00:03:45,597
Did Florence leave already?

43
00:03:45,597 --> 00:03:47,752
Yes, Sir, she left already.

44
00:03:47,752 --> 00:03:49,594
Well, call the recruitment agency.

45
00:03:49,594 --> 00:03:52,500
- We need a cook now...
- Don Ferell...

46
00:03:52,501 --> 00:03:56,666
Double their salary,
and talk to the best cooks.

47
00:03:56,667 --> 00:03:59,233
Once they find out how big the salary is,
they'll agree to work for us.

48
00:03:59,234 --> 00:04:00,184
Sir?

49
00:04:00,184 --> 00:04:01,540
Yes?

50
00:04:01,540 --> 00:04:04,032
Can I please speak freely?

51
00:04:04,033 --> 00:04:06,078
And please listen.

52
00:04:06,078 --> 00:04:09,445
She wants to say goodbye to you,

53
00:04:09,445 --> 00:04:13,094
but you made orders not to disturb you,

54
00:04:13,094 --> 00:04:15,641
that's why she didn't insist.

55
00:04:15,641 --> 00:04:20,925
But before she went home,
she left you a message.

56
00:04:24,696 --> 00:04:26,865
<i>Hello, Grandfather Garp.</i>

57
00:04:26,865 --> 00:04:30,004
<i>Ma'am Serafica said you're busy,</i>

58
00:04:30,004 --> 00:04:32,804
<i>that's why I won't disturb you
and say goodbye.</i>

59
00:04:32,804 --> 00:04:35,907
<i>But the reason why I'm doing this video</i>

60
00:04:35,907 --> 00:04:41,880
<i>is to show you
how to cook your favorite chopsuey recipe!</i>

61
00:04:41,880 --> 00:04:44,402
<i>But before we start, Grandfather Garp,</i>

62
00:04:44,402 --> 00:04:47,616
<i>we need to do a magic ritual.</i>

63
00:04:47,616 --> 00:04:49,020
<i>That's important.</i>

64
00:04:49,020 --> 00:04:51,131
<i>Game.</i>

65
00:04:51,131 --> 00:04:53,391
Join me.

66
00:05:00,832 --> 00:05:02,434
Did you do that?

67
00:05:02,434 --> 00:05:06,039
Maybe you're thinking right now
that I'm a fool,

68
00:05:06,039 --> 00:05:09,494
but that's the most important thing
before we start cooking,

69
00:05:09,494 --> 00:05:11,450
so that our heart is ready to cook.

70
00:05:11,450 --> 00:05:16,235
Because in cooking, the heart is important.

71
00:05:16,235 --> 00:05:20,477
So after our ritual,
are you ready, Grandfather Garp?

72
00:05:20,477 --> 00:05:24,177
Are you ready to cook your favorite chopsuey?

73
00:05:24,177 --> 00:05:26,255
Yes, ready.

74
00:05:26,255 --> 00:05:28,193
So first, Grandfather Garp,

75
00:05:28,193 --> 00:05:33,831
we need to wash our hands
so our food will be clean.

76
00:05:39,271 --> 00:05:44,342
There you go. Next, let's heat up our pan.

77
00:05:46,011 --> 00:05:51,183
But our fire should be just moderate...

78
00:05:51,183 --> 00:05:53,725
there, just like that.

79
00:05:53,725 --> 00:05:57,919
And then, let's wait to have energy,

80
00:05:57,919 --> 00:06:00,892
something like,
"Let's go, Florencia. Let's cook now".

81
00:06:00,892 --> 00:06:03,527
That's it. So, let's just wait.

82
00:06:06,064 --> 00:06:08,533
Game. It's now calling me, Grandfather Garp.

83
00:06:08,533 --> 00:06:12,237
Now, if you can feel the energy
like what I'm feeling right now,

84
00:06:12,237 --> 00:06:16,040
let's add some oil.

85
00:06:17,458 --> 00:06:23,315
There you go.
Let's add onions and saute them.

86
00:06:23,315 --> 00:06:28,920
And once this is okay,
let's put the snow peas,

87
00:06:28,920 --> 00:06:31,622
everybody's favorite.

88
00:06:31,622 --> 00:06:38,316
Then, add a little water,
and then, sesame oil.

89
00:06:38,316 --> 00:06:40,932
And then, Grandfather Garp, once that's okay,

90
00:06:40,932 --> 00:06:44,169
let's add my secret ingredient.

91
00:06:44,169 --> 00:06:45,203
Here it is.

92
00:06:45,203 --> 00:06:46,905
Are you ready, Grandfather Garp?

93
00:06:46,905 --> 00:06:49,040
Grand reveal!

94
00:06:49,741 --> 00:06:51,917
It's roasted chicken.

95
00:06:51,917 --> 00:06:55,982
<i>Just shred it into pieces
and mix it with what you are cooking.</i>

96
00:06:55,982 --> 00:07:02,420
<i>Add a little salt and crushed pepper,
you now have chopsuey!</i>

97
00:07:03,288 --> 00:07:07,225
Thank you so much, Grandfather Garp.

98
00:07:07,225 --> 00:07:11,463
I will never forget you
and all the people here.

99
00:07:11,463 --> 00:07:16,534
You're the best grandfather that I've met.

100
00:07:16,534 --> 00:07:20,672
Oh, Grandfather Garp,
don't post this on social media.

101
00:07:20,672 --> 00:07:24,241
My real grandfather might see this
and feel bad about me.

102
00:07:28,420 --> 00:07:30,766
That's all. Thank you.

103
00:07:30,766 --> 00:07:32,650
Bye!

104
00:07:43,395 --> 00:07:47,432
No wonder Florence is not
replying to my text messages.

105
00:07:47,432 --> 00:07:49,934
And I was calling her
the whole morning earlier.

106
00:07:49,934 --> 00:07:51,369
Should we go to her?

107
00:07:51,369 --> 00:07:53,813
Let's talk to her, and let's ask her

108
00:07:53,813 --> 00:07:57,208
if there's something we can help her with.

109
00:07:57,208 --> 00:07:59,711
I don't think that's a good idea.

110
00:07:59,711 --> 00:08:02,934
I agree.
It looks like her parents are not happy.

111
00:08:02,934 --> 00:08:06,938
She didn't explain to her parents
that she was cooking for us.

112
00:08:06,938 --> 00:08:09,841
They thought she was cooking for little kids.

113
00:08:09,841 --> 00:08:14,979
Well, to be fair,
you guys act like toddlers sometimes, right?

114
00:08:14,979 --> 00:08:16,948
Wow.

115
00:08:16,948 --> 00:08:18,216
For real.

116
00:08:18,216 --> 00:08:19,417
Wow.

117
00:08:19,417 --> 00:08:21,686
- We don't.
- Right?

118
00:08:21,686 --> 00:08:24,255
So, what will happen to Florence?

119
00:08:24,255 --> 00:08:26,891
Will she be okay?

120
00:08:26,891 --> 00:08:31,762
Grandfather Garp said
that she can continue her studies.

121
00:08:32,564 --> 00:08:34,766
After all, she's a scholar.

122
00:08:34,766 --> 00:08:38,436
And the scholarship will be valid,
unless she has a failing mark

123
00:08:38,436 --> 00:08:42,941
or she violated school rules
and got suspended.

124
00:08:42,941 --> 00:08:45,477
But the bigger question is,

125
00:08:45,477 --> 00:08:48,646
what will happen to Florence and Nero?

126
00:08:48,646 --> 00:08:51,483
The last time I saw Florence...

127
00:08:51,483 --> 00:08:53,418
she looked really heartbroken.

128
00:08:53,418 --> 00:08:56,921
If you were given mixed signals
like what Nero did.

129
00:08:56,921 --> 00:08:58,256
Right?

130
00:08:58,256 --> 00:09:01,292
At the end of the day, Nero led Florence on.

131
00:09:01,292 --> 00:09:05,461
Now, Florence is gone from his life...
for good.

132
00:09:07,332 --> 00:09:09,099
That's sad.

133
00:09:14,194 --> 00:09:16,729
So, what happens now?

134
00:09:35,087 --> 00:09:36,888
That's enough.

135
00:09:38,263 --> 00:09:40,064
Why do you have this?

136
00:09:40,064 --> 00:09:42,099
What are you doing here?

137
00:09:44,066 --> 00:09:46,468
What are you doing here?

138
00:09:48,640 --> 00:09:51,476
I'm sorry... I didn't mean it.

139
00:09:51,476 --> 00:09:54,044
It suddenly caught fire.

140
00:09:56,681 --> 00:09:58,816
Believe me, Grandfather.

141
00:09:58,816 --> 00:10:01,219
Even if I'm calm...

142
00:10:01,219 --> 00:10:04,689
I don't want to see the face of this woman.

143
00:10:04,689 --> 00:10:08,759
So please... Grandfather, throw her out.

144
00:10:40,224 --> 00:10:41,992
Let's go, Florence.

145
00:11:30,975 --> 00:11:32,910
She's my girlfriend.

146
00:11:47,003 --> 00:11:50,739
Shall we, my... Chummy pie?

147
00:11:55,268 --> 00:11:57,270
Let's share.

148
00:11:58,870 --> 00:12:01,438
Okay, you can use the other side.

149
00:12:03,620 --> 00:12:06,088
Your head is big.

150
00:12:07,812 --> 00:12:09,013
Let's adjust.

151
00:12:09,013 --> 00:12:10,481
Did I just offend you?

152
00:12:10,481 --> 00:12:12,250
- Or not?
- Not really.

153
00:12:12,250 --> 00:12:13,584
Just for tonight...

154
00:12:13,584 --> 00:12:15,119
- Tomorrow...
- The sky is so beautiful.

155
00:12:15,119 --> 00:12:16,954
Come on, let's look at it.

156
00:12:59,764 --> 00:13:02,499
What? Game?

157
00:13:05,984 --> 00:13:07,785
What?

158
00:13:10,675 --> 00:13:12,366
What?

159
00:13:21,460 --> 00:13:24,855
What? Don't you even
have a perimeter defense?

160
00:13:36,435 --> 00:13:38,302
What do you think?

161
00:13:50,100 --> 00:13:52,400
[DNA Paternity Report]
[Florence Dela Cruz, Lorenzo Almero]

162
00:13:53,033 --> 00:13:58,534
[Probability of Paternity: 99.999%]

163
00:14:12,637 --> 00:14:15,405
Don Rogelio, you called for me?

164
00:14:16,101 --> 00:14:17,902
Talk to our guys.

165
00:14:18,810 --> 00:14:21,712
I want to know everything
about Florence Dela Cruz.

166
00:14:21,712 --> 00:14:24,382
Everything about her.

167
00:14:24,382 --> 00:14:27,873
How did she grow up?
Who are her parents she grew up with?

168
00:14:27,873 --> 00:14:32,577
I want to know everything
about my grandchild.

169
00:14:33,691 --> 00:14:36,712
So that I will be ready when she comes back.

170
00:14:36,712 --> 00:14:38,175
Yes, Sir.

171
00:14:50,159 --> 00:14:52,861
So, what's your plan?

172
00:14:54,759 --> 00:14:56,661
Don't tell me that's it, bro.

173
00:14:56,661 --> 00:14:59,029
You'll just let Florence be?

174
00:15:00,765 --> 00:15:03,301
I've hurt her so much.

175
00:15:03,301 --> 00:15:06,237
That's why maybe I'm the last person
she wants to see.

176
00:15:06,237 --> 00:15:09,173
But we both know
you didn't do that to hurt her.

177
00:15:09,173 --> 00:15:12,142
We know you were doing that to protect her.

178
00:15:13,244 --> 00:15:16,380
I already talked to Antonia.
I know what she did.

179
00:15:16,380 --> 00:15:18,216
Honestly, I was surprised.

180
00:15:18,216 --> 00:15:20,384
It's so out of character of her,

181
00:15:20,384 --> 00:15:23,554
but I guess she had her valid reasons.

182
00:15:23,554 --> 00:15:26,257
That gives you a very valid reason as well.

183
00:15:26,257 --> 00:15:29,359
You know, if Florence knows why you did it,
she'll understand.

184
00:15:31,162 --> 00:15:34,065
If you can sacrifice to protect her,

185
00:15:34,065 --> 00:15:36,768
then you should not give up on
trying to make her understand.

186
00:15:36,768 --> 00:15:39,836
You did this not to hurt her,
but to protect her.

187
00:15:41,205 --> 00:15:43,074
She's one of a kind, bro.

188
00:15:43,074 --> 00:15:44,976
Don't give her up.

189
00:15:44,976 --> 00:15:47,978
Or else, you'd regret this
for the rest of your life.

190
00:16:37,528 --> 00:16:39,030
Good morning, Mother!

191
00:16:39,030 --> 00:16:41,465
Good morning, Father!

192
00:16:45,002 --> 00:16:47,137
Good morning, Florence.

193
00:16:56,480 --> 00:16:58,137
Good morning, Florence.

194
00:16:58,933 --> 00:17:01,277
What are you doing here?

195
00:17:01,277 --> 00:17:05,209
Florence, he's been waiting here
for quite some time.

196
00:17:05,209 --> 00:17:08,212
He said you owe him dinner,

197
00:17:08,212 --> 00:17:09,739
because in the auction,

198
00:17:09,739 --> 00:17:12,906
he bid a million pesos
for you to cook for him.

199
00:17:12,906 --> 00:17:14,384
Is that true?

200
00:17:15,478 --> 00:17:17,480
One million pesos.

201
00:17:18,738 --> 00:17:21,791
And if any of you are thinking to outbid me,

202
00:17:21,792 --> 00:17:24,161
don't try anymore.

203
00:17:24,161 --> 00:17:27,331
Because I won't waste this chance

204
00:17:27,331 --> 00:17:30,100
to be with an important person to me.

205
00:17:30,735 --> 00:17:34,771
I won't waste the chance
to be with you again, Florence.

206
00:17:38,109 --> 00:17:40,011
That's for charity.

207
00:17:40,011 --> 00:17:41,946
It'll be a pity if I take back
the one million pesos

208
00:17:41,946 --> 00:17:44,548
if Florence won't cook for me.

209
00:17:44,548 --> 00:17:46,617
See? It's for charity.

210
00:17:46,617 --> 00:17:48,719
Just grant his request
and think about all the people

211
00:17:48,719 --> 00:17:50,954
that will benefit from that donation.

212
00:17:53,939 --> 00:17:55,706
Well...

213
00:17:57,428 --> 00:18:01,632
A deal is a deal,
so I'll honor what we've agreed upon.

214
00:18:01,632 --> 00:18:06,069
So when, how, and where do you want
to have dinner, Mr. Ferell?

215
00:18:06,704 --> 00:18:10,408
Actually, you don't have to cook for me.

216
00:18:10,408 --> 00:18:13,210
I just want to talk to you.

217
00:18:13,210 --> 00:18:14,945
Is this one of your favors?

218
00:18:14,945 --> 00:18:21,018
No, but before, you asked me
for a minute to explain yourself.

219
00:18:21,018 --> 00:18:22,920
That's what I'm going to ask from you.

220
00:18:22,920 --> 00:18:25,722
A minute to explain myself.

221
00:18:33,946 --> 00:18:38,069
So do you think
Nero will try to win her back?

222
00:18:38,069 --> 00:18:42,173
I talked to him last night,
and I hope it's enough to push him.

223
00:18:42,173 --> 00:18:44,141
This is exciting.

224
00:18:44,141 --> 00:18:48,012
I hope they patch things up,
and I hope they'll end up together.

225
00:18:48,012 --> 00:18:50,281
So there'll be a sequel to this story.

226
00:18:50,281 --> 00:18:52,316
- Yeah.
- Sequel...

227
00:18:52,316 --> 00:18:55,619
If they patch things up and end up together,
there's no more sequel.

228
00:18:55,619 --> 00:18:58,188
Technically, the story is finished.

229
00:18:59,757 --> 00:19:01,025
Troy has a point.

230
00:19:01,025 --> 00:19:03,060
Exactly.

231
00:19:03,060 --> 00:19:08,399
You talk as if Nero and Florence
are characters in a book.

232
00:19:08,399 --> 00:19:11,068
Well, what's important now

233
00:19:11,068 --> 00:19:15,639
is that they have a chance
to fix their relationship, right?

234
00:19:15,639 --> 00:19:17,541
That's right! That's how one should think.

235
00:19:17,541 --> 00:19:19,843
You're really the best, Lina.

236
00:19:34,225 --> 00:19:36,326
Can I join you guys?

237
00:19:37,728 --> 00:19:39,997
Oh guys, by the way, my treat.

238
00:19:39,997 --> 00:19:43,067
Let's go to Paris again.

239
00:19:43,067 --> 00:19:45,002
Why don't we go to Korea instead?

240
00:19:45,002 --> 00:19:47,905
Oh my God, BTS...

241
00:19:47,905 --> 00:19:49,940
We just went to Korea last year.

242
00:19:49,940 --> 00:19:52,309
- Let's go to Paris.
- As in now.

243
00:19:56,180 --> 00:19:57,915
Okay, one minute.

244
00:19:57,915 --> 00:19:59,299
Go.

245
00:20:01,056 --> 00:20:03,220
I like you.

246
00:20:03,220 --> 00:20:05,589
I really like you.

247
00:20:05,589 --> 00:20:07,892
And during the time we were still pretending,

248
00:20:07,892 --> 00:20:10,460
what I was feeling for you, is true.

249
00:20:12,517 --> 00:20:14,352
But...

250
00:20:16,567 --> 00:20:18,368
Just a second.

251
00:20:19,278 --> 00:20:21,835
Can I ask you a favor?

252
00:20:21,835 --> 00:20:23,741
What is it?

253
00:20:23,741 --> 00:20:27,411
Can Aylip stop bothering Florence Dela Cruz?

254
00:20:27,411 --> 00:20:29,346
Break up with her.

255
00:20:29,346 --> 00:20:33,750
Finish whatever it is that you have,
and let's get back together.

256
00:20:34,785 --> 00:20:36,820
Do you think I want to reconcile with you?

257
00:20:36,820 --> 00:20:38,556
Do you think that you have a choice, Nero?

258
00:20:38,556 --> 00:20:41,257
You and I were meant to be together.

259
00:20:42,826 --> 00:20:45,129
I can destroy her.

260
00:20:45,129 --> 00:20:49,133
She lied in front of the school
when she agreed to be your girlfriend.

261
00:20:49,133 --> 00:20:50,901
And I can make a case to the dean,

262
00:20:50,901 --> 00:20:55,472
that's a violation of
the ethical standards of our school.

263
00:20:57,875 --> 00:21:00,177
And the least that could happen is...

264
00:21:00,177 --> 00:21:02,947
it could warrant a suspension.

265
00:21:02,947 --> 00:21:04,915
And if I'm not mistaken,

266
00:21:04,915 --> 00:21:08,551
that suspension could cancel her scholarship.

267
00:21:10,888 --> 00:21:12,922
But I was wrong.

268
00:21:13,528 --> 00:21:18,699
I thought I was protecting you,
but I was hurting you even more.

269
00:21:21,180 --> 00:21:25,835
So I'll ask a favor from you,
so I can prove what I'm feeling.

270
00:21:25,836 --> 00:21:28,439
- And everything...
- Okay, your one minute is over.

271
00:21:28,439 --> 00:21:30,007
Time's up. You can stop now.

272
00:21:30,007 --> 00:21:31,710
Florence...

273
00:21:31,710 --> 00:21:33,067
didn't you even give him a grace period?

274
00:21:33,067 --> 00:21:35,045
Let him finish.

275
00:21:35,045 --> 00:21:39,049
Go ahead, just continue, you left me hanging.

276
00:21:41,485 --> 00:21:43,053
I will do everything

277
00:21:43,053 --> 00:21:47,190
to prove to you
that I deserve to be a part of your life.

278
00:21:51,462 --> 00:21:52,944
Really?

279
00:21:54,498 --> 00:21:57,400
Let's see how far you can go.

280
00:22:05,009 --> 00:22:07,511
Hey, Joshua! That's hands-off.

281
00:22:07,511 --> 00:22:09,780
You might seal the side mirror and tires.

282
00:22:09,780 --> 00:22:11,015
This is safe with us.

283
00:22:11,015 --> 00:22:13,317
- We'll take care of this.
- Keep an eye and do not steal.

284
00:22:13,317 --> 00:22:15,252
- Keep an eye and do not steal.
- We'll take care of it.

285
00:22:15,252 --> 00:22:18,055
- Hey, Ms. Marie, Ms. Rose.
- Florence.

286
00:22:18,055 --> 00:22:19,056
Here it is.

287
00:22:19,056 --> 00:22:21,358
Welcome to my world! This is my world.

288
00:22:21,358 --> 00:22:22,633
It's a bit messy here,
and there are a lot of people.

289
00:22:22,633 --> 00:22:26,163
Everyone knows each other,
like Mr. Dennis and Mr. Gilbert.

290
00:22:26,163 --> 00:22:27,564
Hello.

291
00:22:27,564 --> 00:22:30,668
Life here is simple, but fun.

292
00:22:30,668 --> 00:22:32,236
So it's fun.

293
00:22:32,236 --> 00:22:34,360
Yes, it's fun, but difficult.

294
00:22:34,360 --> 00:22:36,140
And you can't be a weakling here.

295
00:22:36,140 --> 00:22:38,676
Outfits like that is a no here.

296
00:22:38,676 --> 00:22:40,210
You should be tough here.

297
00:22:40,210 --> 00:22:42,379
So? Are you tough?

298
00:22:42,379 --> 00:22:44,147
Yes, of course.

299
00:22:51,188 --> 00:22:52,890
Hello, Ms. Diding.

300
00:22:52,890 --> 00:22:55,359
It looks like
your galunggong fish is fresh today.

301
00:22:55,359 --> 00:22:56,827
Go for galunggong.

302
00:22:56,827 --> 00:22:58,028
We'll help you.

303
00:22:58,028 --> 00:23:00,998
No need, Florence, I can handle this.

304
00:23:00,998 --> 00:23:02,833
Ms. Diding, don't be shy.

305
00:23:02,833 --> 00:23:06,503
My companion here is in top shape.
Nero can handle that.

306
00:23:07,237 --> 00:23:08,572
What are you waiting for?

307
00:23:08,572 --> 00:23:09,907
Go for the gold.

308
00:23:09,907 --> 00:23:12,008
- No problem.
- Go for galunggong.

309
00:23:13,477 --> 00:23:15,245
I can handle that.

310
00:23:20,884 --> 00:23:22,820
That's light. I can carry that.

311
00:23:22,820 --> 00:23:24,121
You should take this one.

312
00:23:24,121 --> 00:23:25,922
Is that it?

313
00:23:34,565 --> 00:23:36,233
Thank you, Nero.

314
00:23:36,233 --> 00:23:37,701
Thank you, Florence.

315
00:23:37,701 --> 00:23:42,138
Hey, your companion is handsome.

316
00:23:44,508 --> 00:23:46,743
You're welcome.

317
00:23:48,278 --> 00:23:50,213
Come on, let's go there.

318
00:23:58,722 --> 00:24:01,425
Sir, can we still ride with you?

319
00:24:01,425 --> 00:24:03,193
It's full already.

320
00:24:03,827 --> 00:24:05,095
When is the next trip?

321
00:24:05,095 --> 00:24:08,532
So this fool can experience
riding a public transportation.

322
00:24:08,532 --> 00:24:09,700
It's a holiday today,

323
00:24:09,700 --> 00:24:12,136
that's why the jeeps are taking tourists
to the falls.

324
00:24:12,136 --> 00:24:15,105
But the other jeeps are probably
on their way.

325
00:24:15,105 --> 00:24:17,040
Okay.

326
00:24:17,040 --> 00:24:18,509
Let's not wait anymore, Florence.

327
00:24:18,509 --> 00:24:19,877
We can sit up there.

328
00:24:19,877 --> 00:24:22,012
- Is that okay?
- Of course.

329
00:24:22,012 --> 00:24:23,780
Just be careful.

330
00:24:34,391 --> 00:24:35,968
Let's go?

331
00:24:37,261 --> 00:24:38,862
Sure.

332
00:24:38,862 --> 00:24:41,064
You can handle that.

333
00:24:41,064 --> 00:24:42,566
Be careful.

334
00:24:42,566 --> 00:24:44,367
Here, hold on to this.

335
00:24:48,906 --> 00:24:50,195
Cool?

336
00:24:52,242 --> 00:24:54,277
Mister, let's go.

337
00:26:18,335 --> 00:26:20,265
They hate me, don't they?

338
00:26:20,983 --> 00:26:22,966
They have a reason to hate you.

339
00:26:22,966 --> 00:26:24,968
You hurt their friend.

340
00:26:24,968 --> 00:26:27,883
The things you do for love.

341
00:26:27,883 --> 00:26:30,952
So, how's your heart?

342
00:26:31,695 --> 00:26:34,832
Well, I thought letting go
would be difficult,

343
00:26:34,832 --> 00:26:36,766
but the truth is...

344
00:26:37,734 --> 00:26:40,357
I seem to be coping pretty well.

345
00:26:40,357 --> 00:26:42,326
That's good.

346
00:26:42,326 --> 00:26:45,195
You act like I'm the only broken-hearted one.

347
00:26:45,195 --> 00:26:47,164
What about you?

348
00:26:47,164 --> 00:26:48,766
Well, there are two ways to react

349
00:26:48,766 --> 00:26:51,735
when you know the person
you love likes someone else.

350
00:26:51,735 --> 00:26:55,439
You can be magnanimous and be happy for her,
which I did.

351
00:26:55,439 --> 00:26:59,115
Or you can be an Antonia, and blackmail him.

352
00:27:02,679 --> 00:27:04,118
Good one.

353
00:27:04,948 --> 00:27:07,084
I can't believe that girl.

354
00:27:07,084 --> 00:27:11,622
The audacity to show herself to us
after what she did to Florence.

355
00:27:11,622 --> 00:27:18,095
Camille, in situations like this,
just think WWFD.

356
00:27:18,095 --> 00:27:20,697
WWFD?

357
00:27:20,697 --> 00:27:22,966
What would Florence do?

358
00:27:23,647 --> 00:27:26,937
I'm sure Florence will forgive her.

359
00:27:26,937 --> 00:27:30,340
Actually, I'm sure she has forgiven Antonia.

360
00:27:30,340 --> 00:27:33,252
If that's the case,
then let's all be like Florence.

361
00:27:33,252 --> 00:27:36,713
Let's open our hearts
and learn to forgive, right?

362
00:27:36,713 --> 00:27:38,982
I still don't like her.

363
00:27:38,982 --> 00:27:41,084
I mean, look...

364
00:27:41,084 --> 00:27:45,255
she's using her charms again to trap Owen.

365
00:27:48,158 --> 00:27:50,160
I'll be honest with you, Antonia.

366
00:27:50,160 --> 00:27:53,263
I really appreciate your capacity to love.

367
00:27:53,263 --> 00:27:57,968
I thought Antonia was all about reputation,
but I was wrong.

368
00:27:57,968 --> 00:28:01,571
There's more to you than meets the eye,
and that's your heart.

369
00:28:04,608 --> 00:28:06,709
We're the same.

370
00:28:07,611 --> 00:28:11,748
Lina, girl.
Why don't you keep an eye on Owen?

371
00:28:11,748 --> 00:28:15,052
I think you two will be perfect together.

372
00:28:15,052 --> 00:28:16,820
I agree.

373
00:28:16,820 --> 00:28:18,589
We'll set you up with him.

374
00:28:18,589 --> 00:28:20,357
Troy will help us.

375
00:28:20,357 --> 00:28:21,358
Yeah.

376
00:28:21,358 --> 00:28:25,496
Troy, help us set Lina up with Owen.

377
00:28:25,496 --> 00:28:26,958
Sure.

378
00:28:27,673 --> 00:28:29,399
Yippee!

379
00:28:41,613 --> 00:28:46,951
Oh well... For us with a heart that loves...

380
00:28:48,018 --> 00:28:50,353
but is unlucky in love.

381
00:28:54,509 --> 00:28:57,177
I think you should
just say sorry to them as well.

382
00:29:08,205 --> 00:29:09,673
Hey.

383
00:29:09,673 --> 00:29:10,908
"Oh, hey"?

384
00:29:10,908 --> 00:29:13,543
That's all you can say, "oh, hey"?

385
00:29:15,145 --> 00:29:16,346
Did I say something wrong?

386
00:29:16,346 --> 00:29:19,011
It seems you're so dense
about what's happening.

387
00:29:19,011 --> 00:29:21,151
What are you talking about?

388
00:29:21,151 --> 00:29:25,756
What I'm saying is,
do you agree to set me up with Owen?

389
00:29:25,756 --> 00:29:27,824
Why? Is it bad?

390
00:29:27,824 --> 00:29:29,960
Is it prohibited?

391
00:29:29,960 --> 00:29:32,462
We don't have a relationship.

392
00:29:35,432 --> 00:29:37,034
You're right.

393
00:29:37,034 --> 00:29:39,703
Maybe I should be dating someone else,

394
00:29:39,703 --> 00:29:42,839
since we don't have a relationship, right?

395
00:29:50,747 --> 00:29:54,585
Now, get some mangoes,
so we'll have something for dessert later.

396
00:29:54,585 --> 00:29:56,687
Okay, which one?

397
00:29:56,687 --> 00:29:58,355
This one?

398
00:29:58,355 --> 00:30:01,191
No, that's not good. It has patches.
Get the other one.

399
00:30:01,191 --> 00:30:02,192
This one?

400
00:30:02,192 --> 00:30:03,493
No, not that one.

401
00:30:03,493 --> 00:30:06,229
The other one, that one.

402
00:30:06,229 --> 00:30:08,532
- That one.
- This one?

403
00:30:08,532 --> 00:30:10,466
- That's it.
- Are you sure?

404
00:30:30,362 --> 00:30:32,130
Nero!

405
00:30:36,393 --> 00:30:38,395
Ouch...

406
00:30:38,395 --> 00:30:40,252
Hey, are you okay?

407
00:30:40,252 --> 00:30:41,525
- Wait.
- Hey!

408
00:30:41,525 --> 00:30:43,667
- Hey!
- No, don't. Please.

409
00:30:43,667 --> 00:30:46,629
Hey, let's step down here first.
Let it rest first.

410
00:30:46,629 --> 00:30:49,174
- Let's stop for a while.
- I think I sprained my ankle.

411
00:30:49,174 --> 00:30:50,900
- Let's stop first.
- Don't worry, I'm okay.

412
00:30:50,900 --> 00:30:54,410
No, we won't walk first. Just stay there.

413
00:30:56,413 --> 00:30:57,932
Ouch.

414
00:30:57,932 --> 00:31:01,818
Why did you force yourself to get it
when you can't do it?

415
00:31:02,686 --> 00:31:06,522
You said that was delicious.

416
00:31:09,521 --> 00:31:11,789
I will do everything for you.

417
00:31:12,507 --> 00:31:14,708
So I can give you what you want.

418
00:31:24,641 --> 00:31:26,576
Are you okay now?

419
00:31:28,118 --> 00:31:30,914
Nero, I don't think it's just a sprain.

420
00:31:30,914 --> 00:31:33,249
It's like something cracked.

421
00:31:44,828 --> 00:31:48,432
- Ouch!
- Can you walk?

422
00:31:48,432 --> 00:31:50,333
I can... just wait.

423
00:31:50,333 --> 00:31:52,536
We need to get out of here.

424
00:31:52,536 --> 00:31:54,271
Ouch.

425
00:31:54,271 --> 00:31:55,672
Hey! Let's go.

426
00:31:55,672 --> 00:31:57,541
- We're getting soaked already.
- Wait...

427
00:31:57,541 --> 00:32:00,444
Ouch, wait.

428
00:32:00,444 --> 00:32:02,278
Wait...

429
00:32:03,180 --> 00:32:05,215
Wait!

430
00:32:05,215 --> 00:32:07,083
Hey! Hurry.

431
00:32:08,386 --> 00:32:11,655
Just go slowly. Don't force it.

432
00:32:11,655 --> 00:32:13,256
Ouch.

433
00:32:13,256 --> 00:32:15,057
Ouch!

434
00:32:17,527 --> 00:32:19,229
- Slowly.
- Just a little more.

435
00:32:19,229 --> 00:32:20,864
Slowly.

436
00:32:20,864 --> 00:32:22,665
Just a little more.

437
00:32:24,634 --> 00:32:26,903
- Ouch.
- Just a little more.

438
00:32:26,903 --> 00:32:29,438
Don't get your head wet.

439
00:32:30,407 --> 00:32:32,408
Just a little more. Come on.

440
00:32:33,877 --> 00:32:35,645
Just stay there.

441
00:32:55,098 --> 00:32:56,966
What are you doing?

442
00:32:57,701 --> 00:32:59,970
I'm sharing my thermal energy with you

443
00:32:59,970 --> 00:33:02,172
so you won't feel cold and have difficulties.

444
00:33:02,172 --> 00:33:04,974
Just like what I watch on TV.

445
00:33:10,647 --> 00:33:13,416
Hi, you're so pretty.

446
00:33:14,753 --> 00:33:18,556
Oh, that looks so good... so good.

447
00:33:22,463 --> 00:33:24,528
What are you doing here?

448
00:33:24,528 --> 00:33:27,197
I just wanted to say that I'm sorry.

449
00:33:27,197 --> 00:33:29,532
Sorry for what?

450
00:33:31,582 --> 00:33:36,766
I've been really selfish lately,
and I've hurt Florence.

451
00:33:36,766 --> 00:33:39,122
I have no excuse for my behavior.

452
00:33:39,122 --> 00:33:42,868
It was... I was just really being immature.

453
00:33:42,868 --> 00:33:46,344
Shouldn't you be apologizing to Florence.

454
00:33:46,344 --> 00:33:47,944
Right?

455
00:33:47,944 --> 00:33:51,448
After all, you've hurt her.

456
00:33:51,448 --> 00:33:53,650
That was my intention,

457
00:33:53,650 --> 00:33:56,486
but when Owen said that you guys are here,

458
00:33:56,486 --> 00:34:00,290
I assumed that she was here too,
but you're right.

459
00:34:00,290 --> 00:34:04,761
I should be on my way
to apologize to Florence personally.

460
00:34:04,761 --> 00:34:06,363
It's not a good idea.

461
00:34:06,363 --> 00:34:08,098
Why not?

462
00:34:08,098 --> 00:34:11,392
She should apologize to Florence.

463
00:34:12,102 --> 00:34:14,904
Owen meant, maybe it's the wrong timing
to go to Florence.

464
00:34:14,904 --> 00:34:16,373
Maybe she's busy.

465
00:34:16,373 --> 00:34:20,310
I think more accurately, they're both busy.

466
00:34:20,310 --> 00:34:22,612
So Nero is with her right now?

467
00:34:22,612 --> 00:34:23,913
Yes.

468
00:34:23,913 --> 00:34:27,350
Oh my gosh.

469
00:34:27,350 --> 00:34:28,985
I knew it.

470
00:34:28,985 --> 00:34:31,955
Like I'm just thinking about it now,
I'm so thrilled.

471
00:34:31,955 --> 00:34:33,722
Oh my God.

472
00:34:36,726 --> 00:34:42,932
Well, maybe they're very sweet now.

473
00:34:42,932 --> 00:34:46,469
Like, they are ants
because they're super sweet.

474
00:34:46,469 --> 00:34:51,207
Probably, they're holding hands now
while walking.

475
00:34:51,207 --> 00:34:54,444
And then, catching each other's gaze,

476
00:34:54,444 --> 00:34:57,313
and it's like there's this invisible force

477
00:34:57,313 --> 00:35:01,017
that's drawing them closer together.

478
00:35:01,017 --> 00:35:04,454
Close enough for a kiss.

479
00:35:04,454 --> 00:35:08,290
A true love's kiss.

480
00:35:10,239 --> 00:35:13,029
I thought you were planning something evil.

481
00:35:13,029 --> 00:35:14,030
Ouch.

482
00:35:14,030 --> 00:35:18,635
Nero Sebastian Araneta Ferell,
you have the nerve to accuse me of that.

483
00:35:18,635 --> 00:35:21,738
- Whatever, you're on your own.
- Ouch, that hurts!

484
00:35:21,738 --> 00:35:22,872
Hey, wait...

485
00:35:22,872 --> 00:35:25,040
- What's with you?
- Ouch.

486
00:35:26,342 --> 00:35:28,111
Will you really neglect me?

487
00:35:28,111 --> 00:35:30,413
Can't you see I can't walk?

488
00:35:30,413 --> 00:35:33,016
Me? Neglecting you?

489
00:35:33,016 --> 00:35:34,818
So now you're saying I'm neglecting you

490
00:35:34,818 --> 00:35:36,719
when I was so concerned about you earlier,

491
00:35:36,719 --> 00:35:39,656
and now you're thinking ill of me?

492
00:35:39,656 --> 00:35:41,491
Why do you get mad easily?

493
00:35:41,491 --> 00:35:43,493
Why do I get mad easily?

494
00:35:43,493 --> 00:35:45,858
Maybe you've forgotten,
in this part of the story,

495
00:35:45,858 --> 00:35:48,231
you're the one who wronged me.

496
00:35:48,231 --> 00:35:51,201
You shouldn't be joking because
you have no right to joke around.

497
00:35:51,201 --> 00:35:52,763
Ouch.

498
00:36:01,736 --> 00:36:06,260
As for me, I would never buy that pretension

499
00:36:06,260 --> 00:36:08,718
to become boyfriend and girlfriend first.

500
00:36:08,718 --> 00:36:12,755
I mean, it could cause
a lot of complications, right?

501
00:36:12,755 --> 00:36:16,000
With... you know what happened
with Florence and Nero.

502
00:36:16,000 --> 00:36:19,261
They were just pretending
until it became real.

503
00:36:19,261 --> 00:36:22,398
Well, that's why, there's a saying, right?

504
00:36:22,398 --> 00:36:24,200
You can get lost,

505
00:36:24,200 --> 00:36:27,804
but sooner or later,
you'll find your way back into love.

506
00:36:27,804 --> 00:36:29,906
It's so corny.

507
00:36:29,906 --> 00:36:31,842
- Oh...
- Tell me that again, Aldus,

508
00:36:31,842 --> 00:36:34,267
once you've fallen in love with me.

509
00:36:36,642 --> 00:36:38,464
But be careful, guys.

510
00:36:38,464 --> 00:36:40,850
Even if you do find your way to love,

511
00:36:40,850 --> 00:36:45,208
you can still get lost... just like me.

512
00:36:45,208 --> 00:36:49,279
Yeah, spoken like a true villain
of the story.

513
00:36:49,279 --> 00:36:50,680
All right, Camille.

514
00:36:50,680 --> 00:36:52,649
- Yeah.
- But that is fair.

515
00:36:52,649 --> 00:36:54,150
I do deserve that.

516
00:36:54,150 --> 00:36:55,806
You do.

517
00:37:02,625 --> 00:37:04,461
Are you two okay?

518
00:37:04,461 --> 00:37:05,783
Yeah.

519
00:37:06,529 --> 00:37:08,531
Why did you suddenly become quiet?

520
00:37:08,531 --> 00:37:09,833
Yes.

521
00:37:09,833 --> 00:37:16,305
Don't tell me you're just like Mark,
who's always quiet.

522
00:37:17,874 --> 00:37:19,842
Where is your energy?

523
00:37:20,834 --> 00:37:21,667
I'm going home.

524
00:37:21,667 --> 00:37:25,247
Are you going with me
or you'll be staying behind?

525
00:37:27,450 --> 00:37:29,852
You know what, we better leave.

526
00:37:29,852 --> 00:37:32,288
Yeah, we better do that.

527
00:37:32,288 --> 00:37:35,091
Sorry, boys, we'll go ahead.

528
00:37:35,091 --> 00:37:37,406
- See you later.
- Bye.

529
00:37:37,406 --> 00:37:38,747
Bye.

530
00:37:39,796 --> 00:37:44,100
Wait... did I say a bad joke?

531
00:37:44,100 --> 00:37:46,936
I don't think it was you, Tristan.

532
00:37:46,936 --> 00:37:50,973
Maybe there's something going on
between Lina and Troy?

533
00:37:53,376 --> 00:37:56,112
Is Antonia right?

534
00:37:56,112 --> 00:37:59,348
Something is going on between you and Lina?

535
00:38:03,753 --> 00:38:06,823
Bro... where are you going?

536
00:38:06,823 --> 00:38:08,308
Let's go.

537
00:38:09,993 --> 00:38:11,661
What's happening?

538
00:38:11,661 --> 00:38:14,029
Did I do something wrong?

539
00:38:16,533 --> 00:38:18,935
I'm sorry.

540
00:38:18,935 --> 00:38:20,303
You're sorry?

541
00:38:20,303 --> 00:38:23,406
That's where you're good at,
always apologizing.

542
00:38:23,406 --> 00:38:25,842
"Sorry, Florence. I was just joking."

543
00:38:25,842 --> 00:38:28,244
"Sorry, Florence. I didn't mean it."

544
00:38:28,244 --> 00:38:31,514
"Sorry, Florence. I was just protecting you."

545
00:38:31,514 --> 00:38:35,285
"Sorry, Florence, for breaking your heart."

546
00:38:35,285 --> 00:38:38,688
Right? You keep on saying sorry.

547
00:38:38,688 --> 00:38:40,256
To tell you the truth,

548
00:38:40,256 --> 00:38:43,760
I'm already scared to open my heart again.

549
00:38:43,760 --> 00:38:45,361
Because I don't want to hear you saying sorry

550
00:38:45,361 --> 00:38:48,063
because you've hurt me again!

551
00:39:17,227 --> 00:39:19,362
That's always been my problem.

552
00:39:19,362 --> 00:39:22,131
I've been raised to read people well.

553
00:39:22,131 --> 00:39:26,202
But it does come in handy for people like us,

554
00:39:26,202 --> 00:39:31,074
who exist in a world where people
can create their own terrible agendas.

555
00:39:31,074 --> 00:39:33,209
Grandfather Garp shielded us from that.

556
00:39:33,209 --> 00:39:36,313
That's why we're all together in the mansion
and not with our parents,

557
00:39:36,313 --> 00:39:40,583
so we don't get involved with the intricacies
of our family business.

558
00:39:40,583 --> 00:39:42,619
I admire your grandfather.

559
00:39:42,619 --> 00:39:46,089
He really does take care of you guys.

560
00:39:46,089 --> 00:39:49,324
What I can say is that I want that too.

561
00:39:50,526 --> 00:39:52,028
Don't feel bad.

562
00:39:52,028 --> 00:39:53,263
As you've said,

563
00:39:53,263 --> 00:39:55,932
being able to read people
can come in as handy.

564
00:39:55,932 --> 00:39:57,267
Think of it this way,

565
00:39:57,267 --> 00:40:00,637
some of the mutants have powers
to read people's minds.

566
00:40:00,637 --> 00:40:02,071
That's so cool, right?

567
00:40:02,071 --> 00:40:03,840
So cool.

568
00:40:03,840 --> 00:40:07,376
Just like what Uncle Ben said,
it can also be a curse.

569
00:40:24,460 --> 00:40:26,062
You know...

570
00:40:26,062 --> 00:40:30,933
before Nero even realized
that he liked Florence...

571
00:40:30,933 --> 00:40:33,535
I already saw it in his eyes.

572
00:40:34,437 --> 00:40:38,140
And I wanted him to look at me
the same way that he looked at her.

573
00:40:38,808 --> 00:40:41,844
And recap to last week's episode,

574
00:40:41,844 --> 00:40:46,482
fate made me realize
that you can't force love.

575
00:40:49,686 --> 00:40:52,789
Maybe if there's something
that fate taught me,

576
00:40:52,789 --> 00:40:56,859
it's that we really have to give
our best shot when it comes to love.

577
00:40:56,859 --> 00:40:59,262
So is that our mantra?

578
00:40:59,262 --> 00:41:02,932
To give it our best
and expect nothing in return?

579
00:41:02,932 --> 00:41:05,968
Not really, maybe what's more appropriate is,

580
00:41:05,968 --> 00:41:08,271
we give it our best,

581
00:41:08,271 --> 00:41:11,507
and hope that someone will return the favor.

582
00:41:11,507 --> 00:41:14,143
Keep hoping, keep believing.

583
00:41:14,143 --> 00:41:15,745
And someday...

584
00:41:15,745 --> 00:41:20,083
someone will come along
who will love us honestly and truthfully.

585
00:41:20,083 --> 00:41:22,952
You really have a way with your words, Owen.

586
00:41:22,952 --> 00:41:26,222
I'm surprised Florence didn't fall for you,

587
00:41:26,222 --> 00:41:29,826
because if I were her...

588
00:41:29,826 --> 00:41:33,463
I would've fallen for your sweet words.

589
00:41:33,463 --> 00:41:36,518
It would've been so easy for me
to fall in love with you.

590
00:41:38,801 --> 00:41:40,803
I mean... no, that's not what I mean.

591
00:41:40,803 --> 00:41:43,713
I'm not implying that I will fall for you.

592
00:41:44,574 --> 00:41:45,875
Ouch.

593
00:41:45,875 --> 00:41:49,979
No, I'll really fall for you.

594
00:41:49,979 --> 00:41:51,338
Really?

595
00:41:52,150 --> 00:41:53,983
You know, I probably should go.

596
00:41:53,983 --> 00:41:55,551
It was really nice seeing you.

597
00:41:55,551 --> 00:41:57,619
I'll see you later.

598
00:42:02,258 --> 00:42:03,793
Hey!

599
00:42:03,793 --> 00:42:05,395
Nero Sebastian Araneta Ferell,

600
00:42:05,395 --> 00:42:08,463
are you really going to leave
as if nothing happened?

601
00:42:09,232 --> 00:42:10,333
What?

602
00:42:10,333 --> 00:42:12,301
You're leaving, that's just about it?

603
00:42:12,301 --> 00:42:15,104
I'm pissed whenever I see you.
Do you know why?

604
00:42:15,104 --> 00:42:17,940
Because I remember what you did to me.

605
00:42:17,940 --> 00:42:21,744
But it doesn't mean
that I don't want to see you anymore.

606
00:42:21,744 --> 00:42:26,315
It doesn't mean
that you shouldn't show yourself and leave.

607
00:42:27,283 --> 00:42:30,119
And that doesn't mean...

608
00:42:30,119 --> 00:42:33,289
that all my feelings for you
will just go away.

609
00:42:33,289 --> 00:42:34,660
What?
